<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
  <title><%= typeof title !== 'undefined' ? title : 'ATI ZMATF Assessment' %></title>

  <%#
    CSRF token for AJAX. public/js/assessment.js reads this and sends it as
    the X-CSRF-Token header on POST /assessment/save-answer.
    Forms use the hidden _csrf input instead.
  %>
  <% if (typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' && csrfToken) { %>
  <meta name="csrf-token" content="<%= csrfToken %>">
  <% } %>

  <%#
    TYPEFACES — self-hosted.

    Drop these subsetted woff2 files into public/fonts/:
      source-serif-4-600.woff2
      fira-sans-400.woff2   fira-sans-650.woff2
      ibm-plex-mono-400.woff2   ibm-plex-mono-600.woff2

    All three families are OFL-licensed and free to self-host. Until the files
    are present the @font-face rules in style.css fail silently and the humanist
    system fallbacks take over, so the app renders correctly either way.

    Self-hosting removes a render-blocking third-party round trip on the
    variable connectivity this cohort works over, and lets the CSP in server.js
    drop fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com entirely.

    To use Google Fonts as an interim bridge instead, uncomment the two links
    below. The CSP in server.js already permits both origins.

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Source+Serif+4:wght@600&family=Fira+Sans:wght@400;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;600&display=swap">
  %>
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/fira-sans-400.woff2" crossorigin>
  <link rel="preload" as="font" type="font/woff2" href="/fonts/source-serif-4-600.woff2" crossorigin>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/style.css">
</head>
<body>

  <a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to main content</a>

  <%#
    NAVIGATION
    Variants are driven by an optional `nav` local so a single layout serves
    every screen. Routes may pass:

      nav: 'none'                        no bar (login, landing)
      nav: 'assessment'                  seal + title + counter + timer
      nav: 'admin'                       seal + title + admin links
      navTitle, navCounter, navDeadline  optional detail

    Omitting `nav` gives the plain institutional bar.
  %>
  <% const navVariant = typeof nav !== 'undefined' ? nav : 'default'; %>
  <% if (navVariant !== 'none') { %>
  <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Primary">
    <div class="site-nav-inner">
      <a href="/" class="row" style="text-decoration:none;gap:10px">
        <span class="nav-seal" aria-hidden="true">A</span>
        <span class="nav-title" style="color:#E6EBE4">
          <%= typeof navTitle !== 'undefined' ? navTitle : 'ATI ZMATF' %>
        </span>
      </a>

      <span class="row-end"></span>

      <% if (navVariant === 'assessment') { %>
        <% if (typeof navCounter !== 'undefined') { %>
          <span class="font-mono" style="font-size:13px;color:#B4C0B7"><%= navCounter %></span>
        <% } %>
        <%#
          The countdown never pulses, flashes, or turns red. public/js/timer.js
          adds .is-low at the two-minute mark, which shifts it to a calm amber
          and stops there. Manufacturing anxiety during a timed assessment is a
          design failure, not a feature.

          data-deadline is the server-issued ISO deadline. The client renders
          from it but the server remains authoritative on expiry.

          data-now is the server's own clock at render time. timer.js diffs it
          against the browser clock and applies the offset to every reading, so
          a participant with a skewed system clock still sees the true remaining
          time. Optional; omit and the browser clock is trusted.
        %>
        <span class="timer-display font-mono"
              id="assessment-timer"
              role="timer"
              aria-live="off"
              <% if (typeof navDeadline !== 'undefined') { %>data-deadline="<%= navDeadline %>"<% } %>
              <% if (typeof navNow !== 'undefined') { %>data-now="<%= navNow %>"<% } %>>
          --:--
        </span>
        <span class="visually-hidden" id="timer-announcer" aria-live="polite"></span>

      <% } else if (navVariant === 'admin') { %>
        <a href="/admin/dashboard">Dashboard</a>
        <a href="/admin/participants">Roster</a>
        <a href="/admin/analytics">Analytics</a>
        <form method="POST" action="/logout" style="display:inline">
          <% if (typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' && csrfToken) { %>
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <% } %>
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-dark">Sign out</button>
        </form>

      <% } else if (typeof user !== 'undefined' && user) { %>
        <span class="font-mono" style="font-size:12px;color:#9CAAA1">
          #<%= user.participant_number %>
        </span>
        <form method="POST" action="/logout" style="display:inline">
          <% if (typeof csrfToken !== 'undefined' && csrfToken) { %>
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
          <% } %>
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-dark">Sign out</button>
        </form>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </nav>
  <% } %>

  <main class="page" id="main-content">
    <%#
      Flash messaging. Routes may set `error` or `success` as plain strings.
      Errors state what went wrong and how to fix it.
    %>
    <% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %>
      <div class="container" style="padding-top:var(--sp-4)">
        <div class="alert alert-danger" role="alert"><%= error %></div>
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <% if (typeof success !== 'undefined' && success) { %>
      <div class="container" style="padding-top:var(--sp-4)">
        <div class="alert alert-success" role="status"><%= success %></div>
      </div>
    <% } %>

    <%- body %>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container row">
      <span class="font-mono" style="font-size:12px">
        &copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Africa Transformational Initiative
      </span>
      <span class="row-end"></span>
      <span class="font-mono" style="font-size:11px;color:#6F7E75">
        ZMATF Executive Training Programme
      </span>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <%#
    Page scripts. Routes opt in via a `scripts` array of paths, e.g.
      scripts: ['/js/timer.js', '/js/assessment.js']
    Nothing is loaded globally, so the landing and login screens ship no JS.
  %>
  <% if (typeof scripts !== 'undefined' && Array.isArray(scripts)) { %>
    <% scripts.forEach(function (src) { %>
      <script src="<%= src %>" defer></script>
    <% }); %>
  <% } %>
</body>
</html>
